3125 6.9375 \nL 24.03125 20.21875 \nL 20.015625 33.296875 \nQ 19.046875 36.625 17.390625 36.625 \nQ 15.921875 36.625 14.25 35.109375 \nQ 12.59375 33.59375 11.921875 32.328125 \nQ 11.53125 32.328125 10.9375 33.109375 \nQ 10.359375 33.890625 10.359375 34.28125 \nQ 10.640625 35.9375 13.953125 39.203125 \nQ 17.28125 42.484375 20.3125 42.484375 \nz\n\" id=\"CrimsonText-Italic-120\"></path>\n     </defs>\n     <g transform=\"translate(277.443926 244.798528)scale(0.15 -0.15)\">\n      <use xlink:href=\"#CrimsonText-Italic-120\"></use>\n     </g>\n    </g>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"line2d_1\">\n    <path clip-path=\"url(#pcfd5fbe2c1)\" d=\"M 63.03256 69.188665 \nL 262.729982 241.848163 \nL 262.729982 241.848163 \n\" style=\"fill:none;stroke:#000000;stroke-linecap:square;stroke-width:2.3;\"></path>\n   </g>\n  </g>\n </g>\n <defs>\n  <clipPath id=\"pcfd5fbe2c1\">\n   <rect height=\"260.82\" width=\"270.55209\" x=\"22.675986\" y=\"7.2\"></rect>\n  </clipPath>\n </defs>\n</svg>\n<div role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Long description for graph of a line\" class=\"sr-only\"><ul><li>The line slants gradually down from left to right.</li>\n<li>The line passes through the following approximate points:<br>\n<ul>\n<li>(0 comma 136)</li>\n<li>(158 comma 0)</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul></div></figure></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">A certain open star cluster contains M-type stars and K-type stars. The estimated total mass of M-type and K-type stars in this open star cluster is <math alttext=\"127,882 quettagrams\"><mrow><mn>127,882</mn></mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>quettagrams</mtext></math>. The graph shown models the possible combinations of the number of M-type stars, <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math>, and K-type stars, <math alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi>\n</math>, that could be in this open star cluster if all the M-type stars have the same estimated mass and all the K-type stars have the same estimated mass. Based on the graph, which of the following is closest to the estimated mass, in quettagrams, of each M-type star in this cluster?</p>","keys":["765b9918-d1b6-4fa2-b0a5-42fc28ef7ede"],"answerOptions":[{"id":"765b9918-d1b6-4fa2-b0a5-42fc28ef7ede","content":"<p><math alttext=\"811\"><mn>811</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"73aaae1d-508b-423b-b76a-65d5c05df6cb","content":"<p><math alttext=\"938\"><mn>938</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"03f69d84-a2f8-4fd3-a67a-6e230a6695f7","content":"<p><math alttext=\"51,904\"><mn>51,904</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"a6a03714-8c91-4cc7-85f9-de51bd3439c5","content":"<p><math alttext=\"75,978\"><mn>75,978</mn>\n</math></p>"}],"rationale":"<p>Choice A is correct. The <em>x</em>-intercept of the graph shown represents the situation in which the cluster contains only M-type stars. Based on the graph, the <em>x</em>-intercept is approximately <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis 158 comma 0 right parenthesis\"><mo>(</mo><mn>158</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo></math>. Therefore, if there are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"0\"><mn>0</mn></math> K-type stars in the cluster, then there are approximately <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"158\"><mn>158</mn></math> M-type stars in the cluster.&nbsp;It&rsquo;s given that the total mass of the stars in this cluster is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"127,882\"><mn>127,882</mn></math> quettagrams. Therefore, the estimated mass of each M-type star is approximately <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"StartFraction 127,882 Over 158 EndFraction\"><mfrac><mn>127,882</mn><mn>158</mn></mfrac></math> quettagrams, or approximately <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"809.38\"><mn>809.38</mn></math> quettagrams. Thus, of the given choices, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"811\"><mn>811</mn></math> is the closest to the estimated mass, in quettagrams, of each M-type star in this cluster.</p>\n<p>Choice B is incorrect. This is the value closest to the estimated mass, in quettagrams, of each K-type star, not each M-type star, in this cluster.</p>\n<p>Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p>Choice D is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>","externalid":"43b52d01-006d-4dbc-b7a8-3187b73ccbce","correct_answer":["A"]},"createDate":1776362727992,"updateDate":1776362727992}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1776362727992, 1776362727992),
    ($SATQ$1a621af4$SATQ$, $SATQ$c72f11a1-3ee5-4aee-a4eb-ef3be78817bb$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$3113a96b-1155-4288-9efd-61983becd38a$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Algebra$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, $SATQ$H.E.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Linear inequalities in one or two variables$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, 6, $SATQ$spr$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">A number <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math> is at most <math alttext="2"><mn>2</mn>
</math> less than <math alttext="3"><mn>3</mn>
</math> times the value of <math alttext="y"><mi>y</mi>
