	<mrow>
		<mo>-</mo>
		<mn>144</mn>
	</mrow>
</mrow>
</math>. Adding this equation to the second equation in the system yields <math alttext="left parenthesis minus 2 a plus 6 right parenthesis x plus left parenthesis minus 2 b plus 2 b right parenthesis y equals left parenthesis negative 144 plus 56 right parenthesis"><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfenced><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>144</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>56</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>, or <math alttext="left parenthesis minus 2 a plus 6 right parenthesis x equals negative 88"><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfenced><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>88</mn></math>. Since <math alttext="left parenthesis 4 comma y right parenthesis"><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is the solution to the system, the value of <math alttext="a"><mi>a</mi>
</math> can be found by substituting <math alttext="4"><mn>4</mn>
</math> for <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math> in this equation, which yields <math alttext="left parenthesis minus 2 a plus 6 right parenthesis left parenthesis 4 right parenthesis equals negative 88"><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mn>4</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>88</mn></math>. Dividing both sides of this equation by <math alttext="4"><mn>4</mn>
</math> yields <math alttext="minus 2 a plus 6 equals negative 22"><mrow>
