ubstituting <math alttext=\"105\"><mn>105</mn>\n</math> for <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math> in this expression yields <math alttext=\"0.44 left parenthesis 105 right parenthesis plus 14.70\"><mn>0.44</mn><mo>(</mo><mn>105</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>14.70</mn></math>, or <math alttext=\"60.90\"><mn>60.90</mn></math>. Therefore, the total pressure exerted on the scuba diver at <math alttext=\"105\"><mn>105</mn>\n</math> feet below sea level is <math alttext=\"60.90 psi\"><mn>60.90</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>psi</mtext></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is incorrect. This is the pressure, in <math alttext=\"psi\"><mtext>psi</mtext></math>, exerted on the scuba diver at sea level, not at <math alttext=\"105\"><mn>105</mn>\n</math> feet below sea level.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is incorrect. This is the rate by which the pressure, in <math alttext=\"psi\"><mtext>psi</mtext></math>, exerted on the scuba diver increases for each foot the scuba diver descends below sea level.</p>","stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The pressure exerted on a scuba diver at sea level is <math alttext=\"14.70 pounds per square inch left parenthesis psi right parenthesis\"><mn>14.70</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>pounds</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>per</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>square</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>inch</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mtext>psi</mtext></mfenced></math>. For each foot the scuba diver descends below sea level, the pressure exerted on the scuba diver increases by <math alttext=\"0.44 psi\"><mn>0.44</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>psi</mtext></math>. What is the total pressure, in <math alttext=\"psi\"><mtext>psi</mtext></math>, exerted on the scuba diver at <math alttext=\"105\"><mn>105</mn>\n</math> feet below sea level?</p>","type":"mcq","correct_answer":["A"]},"createDate":1730147357388,"updateDate":1730147357388}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1730147357388, 1730147357388),
    ($SATQ$1ce51655$SATQ$, $SATQ$85822077-c33d-45ef-bd16-1f8decf34dde$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Algebra$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, $SATQ$H.A.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Linear equations in one variable$SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 4, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p>A bowl contains <math alttext="20"><mn>20</mn>
</math> ounces of water. When the bowl is uncovered, the amount of water in the bowl decreases by <math alttext="1"><mn>1</mn>
</math> ounce every <math alttext="4"><mn>4</mn>
</math> days. If <math alttext="9"><mn>9</mn>
</math> ounces of water remain in this bowl, for how many days has it been uncovered?&nbsp;</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"de5af28f-b9d3-4a09-a35a-28c2c30abe59","content":"<p><math alttext=\"3\"><mn>3</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"45b5639f-cb6e-4513-888a-cc278ba2c2e1","content":"<p><math alttext=\"7\"><mn>7</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"c80a1eb8-820c-43ef-abdf-c037ee55b9e7","content":"<p><math alttext=\"36\"><mn>36</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"97f77309-41e4-4040-946a-88a00cc3f75f","content":"<p><math alttext=\"44\"><mn>44</mn>\n</math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["D"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["97f77309-41e4-4040-946a-88a00cc3f75f"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice D is correct. It&rsquo;s given that the bowl starts with <math alttext="20"><mn>20</mn>
</math> ounces of water and has <math alttext="9"><mn>9</mn>
</math> ounces of water remaining after a period of time has passed. The amount of water the bowl has lost during the time period can be found by subtracting the remaining amount of water from the amount of water the bowl starts with, which yields <math alttext="20 minus 9"><mn>20</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn></math> ounces, or <math alttext="11"><mn>11</mn>
</math> ounces. This means the bowl loses <math alttext="11"><mn>11</mn>
</math> ounces of water during that period of time. It&rsquo;s given that the amount of water decreases by <math alttext="1"><mn>1</mn>
</math> ounce every <math alttext="4"><mn>4</mn>
</math> days. Letting <math alttext="t"><mi>t</mi>
</math> represent the number of days the bowl has been uncovered, it follows that <math alttext="one fourth equals StartFraction 11 Over t EndFraction"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>11</mn><mi>t</mi></mfrac></math>. Multiplying both sides of this equation by <math alttext="4 t"><mrow>
<mn>4</mn>
<mi>t</mi>
</mrow>
</math> yields <math alttext="t equals 44"><mrow>
<mi>t</mi>
<mo>=</mo>
<mn>44</mn>
</mrow>
</math>. Therefore, the bowl has been uncovered for <math alttext="44"><mn>44</mn>
</math> days.&nbsp;</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.&nbsp;</p>
