    ($SATQ$1fe778dc$SATQ$, $SATQ$84a52145-ed23-4de2-9bb6-c1f412e7b1f8$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Algebra$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, $SATQ$H.C.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Linear equations in two variables$SATQ$, $SATQ$E$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">A line in the&nbsp;<em>xy</em>-plane has a slope of&nbsp;<math alttext="negative one half"><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math> and passes through the point&nbsp;<math alttext="left parenthesis 0 comma 3 right parenthesis"><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>. Which equation represents this line?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"a381950a-ada3-43a6-8704-647106fdc714","content":"<p><math alttext=\"y equals minus one half x minus 3\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></math></p>"},{"id":"e9a1e745-a5cf-494e-9222-df510705eaee","content":"<p><math alttext=\"y equals minus one half x plus 3\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></math></p>"},{"id":"3410eb0a-9283-472c-acb7-3d1d5ecea56c","content":"<p><math alttext=\"y equals one half x minus 3\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></math></p>"},{"id":"07c1c838-5f32-41d5-9693-df134d8e19d6","content":"<p><math alttext=\"y equals one half x plus 3\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["B"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["e9a1e745-a5cf-494e-9222-df510705eaee"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice B is correct. A line in the <em>xy</em>-plane with a slope of <math alttext="m"><mi>m</mi>
</math> and a <em>y</em>-intercept of <math alttext="left parenthesis 0 comma b right parenthesis"><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> can be represented by the equation <math alttext="y equals m x plus b"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></math>.&nbsp;It's given that the line has a slope of <math alttext="negative one half"><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>. Therefore, <math alttext="m equals negative one half"><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>. It's also given that the line passes through the point <math alttext="left parenthesis 0 comma 3 right parenthesis"><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>. Therefore,&nbsp;<math alttext="b equals 3"><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math>. Substituting <math alttext="negative one half"><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math> for <math alttext="m"><mi>m</mi>
</math> and <math alttext="3"><mn>3</mn>
</math> for <math alttext="b"><mi>b</mi>
</math> in the equation <math alttext="y equals m x plus b"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></math> yields <math alttext="y equals minus one half x plus 3"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></math>. Therefore, the equation <math alttext="y equals minus one half x plus 3"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></math> represents this line.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is incorrect. This equation represents a line in the <em>xy</em>-plane that passes through the point <math alttext="left parenthesis 0 comma negative 3 right parenthesis"><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>, not <math alttext="left parenthesis 0 comma 3 right parenthesis"><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>.</p>
