<p style="text-align: left;">Choice D is incorrect. This equation represents a line in the <em>xy</em>-plane that has a slope of <math alttext="one half"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>, not <math alttext="negative one half"><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"1fe778dc","external_id":"84a52145-ed23-4de2-9bb6-c1f412e7b1f8","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"d9e11e5b-c0bd-4bc6-91a3-4e0dc8432f33","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"H","domain":"Algebra","skill_cd":"H.C.","skill_desc":"Linear equations in two variables","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":1,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">A line in the&nbsp;<em>xy</em>-plane has a slope of&nbsp;<math alttext=\"negative one half\"><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math> and passes through the point&nbsp;<math alttext=\"left parenthesis 0 comma 3 right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>. Which equation represents this line?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"a381950a-ada3-43a6-8704-647106fdc714","content":"<p><math alttext=\"y equals minus one half x minus 3\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></math></p>"},{"id":"e9a1e745-a5cf-494e-9222-df510705eaee","content":"<p><math alttext=\"y equals minus one half x plus 3\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></math></p>"},{"id":"3410eb0a-9283-472c-acb7-3d1d5ecea56c","content":"<p><math alttext=\"y equals one half x minus 3\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></math></p>"},{"id":"07c1c838-5f32-41d5-9693-df134d8e19d6","content":"<p><math alttext=\"y equals one half x plus 3\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>x</m