<mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></math> yields <math alttext=\"y equals minus one half x plus 3\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></math>. Therefore, the equation <math alttext=\"y equals minus one half x plus 3\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></math> represents this line.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is incorrect. This equation represents a line in the <em>xy</em>-plane that passes through the point <math alttext=\"left parenthesis 0 comma negative 3 right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>, not <math alttext=\"left parenthesis 0 comma 3 right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is incorrect. This equation represents a line in the <em>xy</em>-plane that has a slope of <math alttext=\"one half\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>, not <math alttext=\"negative one half\"><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>, and passes through the point <math alttext=\"left parenthesis 0 comma negative 3 right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>, not <math alttext=\"left parenthesis 0 comma 3 right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is incorrect. This equation represents a line in the <em>xy</em>-plane that has a slope of <math alttext=\"one half\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>, not <math alttext=\"negative one half\"><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>.</p>","stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">A line in the&nbsp;<em>xy</em>-plane has a slope of&nbsp;<math alttext=\"negative one half\"><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math> and passes through the point&nbsp;<math alttext=\"left parenthesis 0 comma 3 right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>. Which equation represents this line?</p>","type":"mcq","correct_answer":["B"]},"createDate":1730147357391,"updateDate":1730147357391}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1730147357391, 1730147357391),
    ($SATQ$208626df$SATQ$, $SATQ$c6ae5b6e-3980-49ff-bd21-fd706a9011aa$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Algebra$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, $SATQ$H.E.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Linear inequalities in one or two variables$SATQ$, $SATQ$E$SATQ$, 3, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: center;"><math alttext="2 script l plus 2 w less than or equals 27"><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant="script">l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>w</mi><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>27</mn></math></p>
<p style="text-align: left;">A rectangle has length&nbsp;<math alttext="script l"><mi mathvariant="script">l</mi></math> and width <math alttext="w"><mi>w</mi>
</math>. The inequality gives the possible values of&nbsp;<math alttext="script l"><mi mathvariant="script">l</mi></math> and <math alttext="w"><mi>w</mi>
</math> for which the perimeter of this rectangle is less than or equal to <math alttext="27"><mn>27</mn>
</math>. Which statement is the best interpretation of <math alttext="left parenthesis script l comma w right parenthesis equals left parenthesis 8 comma 3 right parenthesis"><mfenced><mrow><mi mathvariant="script">l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> in this context?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"0c1bb4dc-d26f-46b7-b72b-b6aec62c8599","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">If the rectangle has length <math alttext=\"3\"><mn>3</mn>\n</math> and width <math alttext=\"8\"><mn>8</mn>\n</math>, its perimeter is less than or equal to <math alttext=\"27\"><mn>27</mn>\n</math>.</p>"},{"id":"d31f1b2e-abfe-4091-a192-9fe581e536d1","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">If the rectangle has length <math alttext=\"8\"><mn>8</mn>\n</math> and width <math alttext=\"3\"><mn>3</mn>\n</math>, its perimeter is less than or equal to <math alttext=\"27\"><mn>27</mn>\n</math>.</p>"},{"id":"d25ecd02-1681-45aa-ba72-964ec546360f","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">If the rectangle has length <math alttext=\"3\"><mn>3</mn>\n</math> and width <math alttext=\"8\"><mn>8</mn>\n</math>, its perimeter is greater than or equal to <math alttext=\"27\"><mn>27</mn>\n</math>.</p>"},{"id":"255379f6-385e-4b43-a553-3536c3565dc1","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">If the rectangle has length <math alttext=\"8\"><mn>8</mn>\n</math> and width <math alttext=\"3\"><mn>3</mn>\n</math>, its perimeter is greater than or equal to <math alttext=\"27\"><mn>27</mn>\n</math>.</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["B"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["d31f1b2e-abfe-4091-a192-9fe581e536d1"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice B is correct. It’s given that a rectangle has length <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="script l"><mi mathvariant="script">l</mi></math> and width <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="w"><mi>w</mi></math>, and the inequality <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="2 script l plus 2 w less than or equals 27"><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant="script">l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>w</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>27</mn></math> gives the possible values of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="script l"><mi mathvariant="script">l</mi></math> and <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="w"><mi>w</mi></math> for which the perimeter of this rectangle is less than or equal to <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="27"><mn>27</mn></math>. To determine the best interpretation of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="left parenthesis script l comma w right parenthesis equals left parenthesis 8 comma 3 right parenthesis"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="script">l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo></math> in this context, the values can be substituted in the given inequality. Substituting <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="8"><mn>8</mn></math> for <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="script l"><mi mathvariant="script">l</mi></math> and <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="3"><mn>3</mn></math> for <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="w"><mi>w</mi></math> in this inequality yields <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="2 left parenthesis 8 right parenthesis plus 2 left parenthesis 3 right parenthesis less than or equals 27"><mn>2</mn><mo>(</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>≤</mo><mn>27</mn></math>, which is equivalent to <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="16 plus 6 less than or equals 27"><mn>16</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>≤</mo><mn>27</mn></math>, or&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="22 less than or equals 27"><mn>22</mn><mo>≤</mo><mn>27</mn></math>. Since this inequality is true,&nbsp;if the rectangle has length <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="8"><mn>8</mn></math> and width <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="3"><mn>3</mn></math>, its perimeter is less than or equal to <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="27"><mn>27</mn></math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is incorrect. The interpretation of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="left parenthesis script l comma w right parenthesis equals left parenthesis 8 comma 3 right parenthesis"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="script">l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo></math> implies that the rectangle has length <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="8"><mn>8</mn></math> and width <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="3"><mn>3</mn></math>, not length <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="3"><mn>3</mn></math> and width <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="8"><mn>8</mn></math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice C is incorrect. The interpretation of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="left parenthesis script l comma w right parenthesis equals left parenthesis 8 comma 3 right parenthesis"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="script">l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo></math> implies that the rectangle has length <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="8"><mn>8</mn></math> and width <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="3"><mn>3</mn></math>, not length <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="3"><mn>3</mn></math> and width <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="8"><mn>8</mn></math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice D is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"208626df","external_id":"c6ae5b6e-3980-49ff-bd21-fd706a9011aa","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"e8d6461d-302b-4a27-b697-02a408b539c4","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"H","domain":"Algebra","skill_cd":"H.E.","skill_desc":"Linear inequalities in one or two variables","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":3,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><math alttext=\"2 script l plus 2 w less than or equals 27\"><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>w</mi><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>27</mn></math></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">A rectangle has length&nbsp;<math alttext=\"script l\"><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi></math> and width <math alttext=\"w\"><mi>w</mi>\n</math>. The inequality gives the possible values of&nbsp;<math alttext=\"script l\"><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi></math> and <math alttext=\"w\"><mi>w</mi>\n</math> for which the perimeter of this rectangle is less than or equal to <math alttext=\"27\"><mn>27</mn>\n</math>. Which statement is the best interpretation of <math alttext=\"left parenthesis script l comma w right parenthesis equals left parenthesis 8 comma 3 right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> in this context?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"0c1bb4dc-d26f-46b7-b72b-b6aec62c8599","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">If the rectangle has length <math alttext=\"3\"><mn>3</mn>\n</math> and width <math alttext=\"8\"><mn>8</mn>\n</math>, its perimeter is less than or equal to <math alttext=\"27\"><mn>27</mn>\n</math>.</p>"},{"id":"d31f1b2e-abfe-4091-a192-9fe581e536d1","content":"<p style=\"