><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>w</mi><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>27</mn></math></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">A rectangle has length&nbsp;<math alttext=\"script l\"><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi></math> and width <math alttext=\"w\"><mi>w</mi>\n</math>. The inequality gives the possible values of&nbsp;<math alttext=\"script l\"><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi></math> and <math alttext=\"w\"><mi>w</mi>\n</math> for which the perimeter of this rectangle is less than or equal to <math alttext=\"27\"><mn>27</mn>\n</math>. Which statement is the best interpretation of <math alttext=\"left parenthesis script l comma w right parenthesis equals left parenthesis 8 comma 3 right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> in this context?</p>","keys":["d31f1b2e-abfe-4091-a192-9fe581e536d1"],"answerOptions":[{"id":"0c1bb4dc-d26f-46b7-b72b-b6aec62c8599","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">If the rectangle has length <math alttext=\"3\"><mn>3</mn>\n</math> and width <math alttext=\"8\"><mn>8</mn>\n</math>, its perimeter is less than or equal to <math alttext=\"27\"><mn>27</mn>\n</math>.</p>"},{"id":"d31f1b2e-abfe-4091-a192-9fe581e536d1","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">If the rectangle has length <math alttext=\"8\"><mn>8</mn>\n</math> and width <math alttext=\"3\"><mn>3</mn>\n</math>, its perimeter is less than or equal to <math alttext=\"27\"><mn>27</mn>\n</math>.</p>"},{"id":"d25ecd02-1681-45aa-ba72-964ec546360f","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">If the rectangle has length <math alttext=\"3\"><mn>3</mn>\n</math> and width <math alttext=\"8\"><mn>8</mn>\n</math>, its perimeter is greater than or equal to <math alttext=\"27\"><mn>27</mn>\n</math>.</p>"},{"id":"255379f6-385e-4b43-a553-3536c3565dc1","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">If the rectangle has length <math alttext=\"8\"><mn>8</mn>\n</math> and width <math alttext=\"3\"><mn>3</mn>\n</math>, its perimeter is greater than or equal to <math alttext=\"27\"><mn>27</mn>\n</math>.</p>"}],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is correct. It’s given that a rectangle has length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"script l\"><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi></math> and width <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"w\"><mi>w</mi></math>, and the inequality <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"2 script l plus 2 w less than or equals 27\"><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>w</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>27</mn></math> gives the possible values of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"script l\"><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"w\"><mi>w</mi></math> for which the perimeter of this rectangle is less than or equal to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"27\"><mn>27</mn></math>. To determine the best interpretation of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis script l comma w right parenthesis equals left parenthesis 8 comma 3 right parenthesis\"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo></math> in this context, the values can be substituted in the given inequality. Substituting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"8\"><mn>8</mn></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"script l\"><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"3\"><mn>3</mn></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"w\"><mi>w</mi></math> in this inequality yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"2 left parenthesis 8 right parenthesis plus 2 left parenthesis 3 right parenthesis less than or equals 27\"><mn>2</mn><mo>(</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>≤</mo><mn>27</mn></math>, which is equivalent to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"16 plus 6 less than or equals 27\"><mn>16</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>≤</mo><mn>27</mn></math>, or&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"22 less than or equals 27\"><mn>22</mn><mo>≤</mo><mn>27</mn></math>. Since this inequality is true,&nbsp;if the rectangle has length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"8\"><mn>8</mn></math> and width <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"3\"><mn>3</mn></math>, its perimeter is less than or equal to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"27\"><mn>27</mn></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is incorrect. The interpretation of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis script l comma w right parenthesis equals left parenthesis 8 comma 3 right parenthesis\"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo></math> implies that the rectangle has length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"8\"><mn>8</mn></math> and width <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"3\"><mn>3</mn></math>, not length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"3\"><mn>3</mn></math> and width <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"8\"><mn>8</mn></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is incorrect. The interpretation of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis script l comma w right parenthesis equals left parenthesis 8 comma 3 right parenthesis\"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo></math> implies that the rectangle has length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"8\"><mn>8</mn></math> and width <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"3\"><mn>3</mn></math>, not length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"3\"><mn>3</mn></math> and width <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"8\"><mn>8</mn></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>","externalid":"c6ae5b6e-3980-49ff-bd21-fd706a9011aa","correct_answer":["B"]},"createDate":1755117017723,"updateDate":1755117017723}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1755117017723, 1755117017723),
